        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-26T16:20:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we anticipate the color format --\u003e format map often not having the renderability required? If so, would it make sense to have the map have one format recommended for non-renderable and one for renderable (with those likely usually being the same values for some color types?)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 937,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 937,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "a5f2ba05264211678268f2a9ec0c027638e93287",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "759f05a0_0ab9f43a",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/mtl/MtlCaps.mm",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 937,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-02T16:31:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not inclined to make changes here because this is just a stop-gap as colortype-related code moves off of Caps.  This had been quite a simple function originally, but the unit tests exposed the existing issues around `renderable` checking for compatibility so this keeps things passing.\n\nIn the future, there will be 3 separate static functions:\n1. PreferredTextureFormats(SkColorType) -\u003e span\u003cTextureFormat\u003e\n2. ColorTypeInfo(TextureFormat) -\u003e SkColorType\n3. GetWriteSwizzle(TextureFormat, SkColorType) -\u003e std::optiona\u003cSwizzle\u003e\n\nThe SkColorType returned that matches a TextureFormat will always be renderable with that format. The preferred texture formats for a color type have to be filtered by both being a supported format, and having a defined write swizzle for the combination of color type and format.\n\nThe only times a write swizzle is not possible is for a gray colortype, or for RGBx color type rendering to a format that still has an alpha channel. So once these functions are in place, this filtering can move up to `Caps::getDefaultSampleableTextureInfo()` and all the `getFormatForColorType()` functions get to be deleted. This is several CLs away, but this code shouldn\u0027t live for that long.",
      "parentUuid": "9e44b4ca_327888f5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 937,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 937,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "a5f2ba05264211678268f2a9ec0c027638e93287",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
